,"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"duplicate","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Duplicate of cded-334b-a742-4082 (closed): the same two facade tests, failing with the same 'I/O operation on closed file' raised from logging emit. Root cause was already diagnosed there - install_stderr_handler (src/rebar/_logging.py) binds a StreamHandler to sys.stderr once and is idempotent by marker, so when an earlier in-process main() installs it while sys.stderr is a pytest capture stream, the handler keeps writing to that stream after it closes. Fix landed via Gerrit 3309; sibling duplicate 4c58-45d4-aaf7-48dc was closed against the same cause.\n\nFiled in error from a checkout pinned 260 commits behind at 2e28d817a7e. Re-checked against current origin/main (38c42c7e70e), where the fix is present. No separate work remains.","timestamp":1793844408416494001}],"completion_expectation":"disposition","created_at":1793844228401534112,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4d3f3b0c-95c4-49d7-b4b1-af0576d03973","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"cded-334b-a742-4082"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nTwo test modules fail when the full suite runs, and pass when run on their own:\n\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py`\n\nThe failure surfaces as a logging teardown error rather than an assertion:\n\n```\nLogging error: I/O operation on closed file\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Confirmed independently twice**, by two separate agents working from different worktrees.\n- **Reproduces on a pristine, unmodified `origin/main` checkout** — it is not caused by any\n  in-flight change.\n- Run in isolation the modules pass: 35/35 observed green.\n- Neither module references the code that was in flight when the failure was first seen, so\n  the coupling is to suite *order*, not to subject matter.\n\nThis is order-dependent and pre-existing. It is filed as a bug rather than retried, per the\nproject rule that a flaky test is a bug to root-cause and never a retry.\n\n## Likely shape (hypotheses, unproven)\n\nEach remains to be distinguished by experiment; none is yet supported by evidence beyond the\nerror text:\n\n1. An earlier test closes a stream that a module-scoped or session-scoped logging handler still\n   holds, so the handler writes to a closed file during this module's teardown.\n2. `caplog`/`capsys` teardown interacts with a handler installed at import time by one of the\n   facade modules and never removed.\n3. A `logging.shutdown()` or handler-removal side effect from an unrelated module leaks across\n   test boundaries.\n\n## Suggested first step\n\nFind the minimal failing pair with `pytest -p no:randomly` plus a bisect over the preceding\nmodules (`--deselect`, or `pytest-bisect`-style halving) to identify the specific predecessor\nthat triggers it. Capture the handler inventory (`logging.root.handlers` and the facade\nloggers' handlers) at the start and end of the predecessor to see which handler's stream is\nclosed and who closed it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The specific predecessor test (or fixture) whose teardown closes the stream is identified\n      and named, with a deterministic two-module reproduction command.\n- [ ] The root cause is fixed at the class level (handler/stream lifetime), not by reordering,\n      skipping, or marking either facade module.\n- [ ] Both facade modules pass in the full `make test` selection and in isolation.\n- [ ] A regression guard exists that would fail if the same handler-lifetime leak is\n      reintroduced.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nReordering the suite, adding `-p no:randomly` to the default selection, or any change that\nhides the ordering dependency rather than removing it.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"338072d2-f9ae-4f12-8421-05b9e02333af","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3694-9ab3-0f40-4753","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Facade attestation tests fail in full-suite order with \"I/O operation on closed file\", pass in isolation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fbbb60a0-5805-430e-8ecc-d6b82e782e23","4d3f3b0c-95c4-49d7-b4b1-af0576d03973","7ba81321-098d-4853-9fb2-2964296f7a12","338072d2-f9ae-4f12-8421-05b9e02333af","cd18b684-f6e3-4d2e-95d7-07cedb6d742d"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793844448143651002,"uuid":"f0c50757-1918-4ee0-a2cf-c33f788a2964"}